142
00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.950
He says, greetings.

143
00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:36.030
My friends and followers were kind enough to alert me that my AV Club reviews have made it onto the podcast as the seventh season reaches its conclusion.

144
00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:40.810
And I want to thank you for bringing back fond memories of my time covering the show.

145
00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:49.570
I've become a media professor in the intervening period, and Rate My Professors has tagged me as a, quote, tough grader.

146
00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.390
So let the record show that I am nothing if not consistent.

147
00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:59.130
In the meantime, I look forward to hearing how Jenna felt about my take on the rest of the season,

148
00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:04.370
and highly recommend she stop reading my reviews in season eight for all of our sakes.

149
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.490
Well, now I can't wait.

150
00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.310
Now I can't wait for you to read them.

151
00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.790
Oh, well, believe me, I'm not stopping.

152
00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:18.610
But he said that we should reach out if we ever want to hear how he feels about the show.

153
00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:27.270
He said, you know, he has different feelings about the show in hindsight, having watched it still many years later rather than in real time.

154
00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.030
And I thought that would be kind of fascinating.

155
00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.470
We have to reach out to him.

156
00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.530
Oh, for sure.

157
00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.870
We have to have a whole opening of the show with Miles McNutt.

158
00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.370
He's Fast Fact 1, 2, and 3.

159
00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:37.470
I agree.

160
00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:43.610
Well, for the premiere of season eight, last week's episode, The List, he gave that episode a B.

161
00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.130
Not so bad.

162
00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.310
Not bad for Miles.

163
00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.230
And he said this.

164
00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:53.710
He said he thought that at the end of the day, the idea of Andy as boss and Robert California as CEO

165
00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.670
