For 5,000 points, you can tattoo anything you want on the stern of the old SS Bernard.

972
00:45:03.230 --> 00:45:04.370
People go crazy.

973
00:45:04.610 --> 00:45:05.070
There's hooting.

974
00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:05.810
There's clapping.

975
00:45:06.730 --> 00:45:06.950
Yes.

976
00:45:07.310 --> 00:45:09.050
And Jim is like, oh, hold up.

977
00:45:09.090 --> 00:45:10.690
And we can pull our points.

978
00:45:10.930 --> 00:45:12.070
And Andy's like, yeah.

979
00:45:12.830 --> 00:45:15.010
Andy, Andy, Andy.

980
00:45:15.530 --> 00:45:16.130
Yeah.

981
00:45:16.130 --> 00:45:20.090
Well, they get there really quickly to the 5,000 points.

982
00:45:20.270 --> 00:45:24.330
I think we should take a break because when we get back, the office is a buzz.

983
00:45:24.510 --> 00:45:25.870
A buzz for sure.

984
00:45:26.210 --> 00:45:36.250
We are back.

985
00:45:36.650 --> 00:45:40.310
Everybody is just on their game right now.

986
00:45:40.510 --> 00:45:43.350
People are answering calls, shouting out stuff.

987
00:45:43.730 --> 00:45:45.550
Papers are being passed around.

988
00:45:46.210 --> 00:45:51.930
So much activity, especially for Dunder Mifflin, when people are mostly at their desks playing solitaire.

989
00:45:52.510 --> 00:45:58.770
We got a fan question from Leah K in Arkansas who said, were there specific directions in

990
00:45:58.770 --> 00:46:02.650
the script about what each character should be doing when the bullpen is suddenly working

991
00:46:02.650 --> 00:46:04.730
hard to reach those 5,000 points?

992
00:46:05.030 --> 00:46:09.670
It feels like some of the characters are just pretending to do work that they wouldn't actually

993
00:46:09.670 --> 00:46:14.070
do, specifically Kevin, who is frantically punching numbers into a calculator.

994
00:46:14.290 --> 00:46:15.410
Kevin, what are you doing?

995
00:46:15.630 --> 00:46:17.010
I love the chaos.

996
00:46:17.170 --> 00:46:18.610
Was it scripted?

997
00:46:18.610 --> 00:46:24.990
Well, Leah, the Kevin portion of this activity was scripted, that he was frantically just

998
00:46:24.990 --> 00:46:27.010
typing random numbers into a calculator.

999
00:46:27.250 --> 00:46:30.390
I have it if you want to hear what it said in the shooting draft for Kevin.

1000
00:46:30.530 --> 00:46:31.230
Oh, please do.

1001
00:46:31.410 --> 00:46:33.270
Because I was actually really curious, too.

1002
00:46:33.530 --> 00:46:34.790
This is what it says.

1003
00:46:35.030 --> 00:46:40.690
